          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<style>\r\nhr.style13 {\r\nheight: 10px;\r\nborder: 0;\r\nbox-shadow: 0 10px 10px -10px #8c8b8b inset;\r\n}\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThe KR10 (or KR11) Knit Contour is used with Silver/Singer/Studio machines. <br>This charting device is a mechanical device that allows the knitter to follow a drawing indicating where shaping should occur. <br><img class=\"ctr\" src=\"/images/glossary/silver_charting_device.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://www.knititnow.com/images/glossary/charting_device_gif.gif\">\r\n\r\n<hr class=\"style13_pink\">\r\n<br><i class=\"fa fa-hand-o-down fa-2x\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i><b> Click the \"spots\" below for the terms describing each part of the device</b>",
