          "title": "{First}, Get Acquainted<br> with your device",
          "slug": "first-get-acquainted-br-with-your-device",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 6348,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\n\r\nThe KR10 included a set of pattern styles for you to use.  They are drawn on paper at various sizes at 1/2 and 1/4 scale.<br>Copy these pattern styles to the  mylar and make any sizing or style changes you need.<br>NOTE:  If you don't have the paper Knit Pattern Set, you can draw your own from hand knitting patterns, or use sewing patterns.<br>\r\nIf using digital a sewing pattern, set the print to 25-50% scale. Then copy the scaled pieces to your mylar.<br><img class=\"ctr\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/122/knit_pattern_set.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\t<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/122/draw.jpg\"><br>\r\nUse a soft pencil or erasable marker to copy/trace the design to your mylar.\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 9722,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Knit Pattern Set",
          "slug": "knit-pattern-set",
          "order": 2,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 6355,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<style>\r\n    .container-border1 {\r\n        border: 2px solid #ccc;\r\n        border-radius: 15px 50px;\r\n        padding-top: 20px;\r\n        padding-right: 20px;\r\n        padding-bottom: 20px;\r\n        padding-left: 20px;\r\n        background-color: white;\r\n    }\r\n\r\nhr.style13 {\r\nheight: 10px;\r\nborder: 0;\r\nbox-shadow: 0 10px 10px -10px #8c8b8b inset;\r\n}\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n\r\n    \r\n\r\n        <div class=\"container-border1\">\r\n\r\n<h4>Stitch Gauge</h4> The stitch gauge is reflected by the <a data-GlossaryId='829' class='glossaryhelp'>Stitch Scale <i class='fa fa-question-circle-o' aria-hidden='true'></i></a>\r\n<h4>Row Gauge</h4>\r\nThe row gauge is controlled by the <span class=\"imagepopup\" data-imagetitle=\"Electronics\" data-image=\"/challenge/images/v2/122/electronics.jpg\"><i class=\"fa fa-picture-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Electronics </span>\r\n\r\n\r\n in the device\r\n\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">\r\n            <ol>\r\n                <li>\r\n                    Establish your stitch and row gauge.</li>\r\n                <li>Use a sewing pattern, dimensions from a knitting pattern, or the included <a data-GlossaryId='831' class='glossaryhelp'>Knit Pattern Set <i class='fa fa-question-circle-o' aria-hidden='true'></i></a>\r\n and draw the shape of the piece you want to knit at either ½ or ¼ scale.</li>\r\n<li>Set the\r\n<span class=\"imagepopup\" data-imagetitle=\"¼ | ½ switch\" data-image=\"/challenge/images/v2/122/quarter.jpg\" width=\"200\"><i class=\"fa fa-picture-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i><b> ¼\r\n | ½\r\nswitch</b></span> </li>\r\n\r\n                <li>Draw the outline of the piece shape on the gridded mylar</li>\r\n<li>Choose the stitch scale to match your stitch gauge in 4\" <em>(10cm)</em></li>\r\n <li>The Stitch scale represents stitches and the needles in work.</li>\r\n                <li>Set your Knit Radar for your row gauge in 4\" <em>(10cm)</em>.</li>\r\n               \r\n                <li>Using the plus and minus key sets the electronics of the device so it advances the mylar as you knit according to your row gauge.<br>\r\n                <li>Follow along where the line matches the divisions on the stitch scale.\r\n                <li>As you knit, the row counter on the device advances the drawing.\r\n            </ol>\r\n        </div>\r\n    <h3>Example</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>I'm planning a newborn baby sweater with a finished chest of 16\" (41cm). I'm using a drawing of the cardigan front that is drawn at 1/2 scale</li>\r\n<li>\r\nMy gauge is 28 stitches and 44 rows = 4\" (10cm)</li>\r\n<li>I'll use the H9 stitch scale and insert it so the 28 sts edge is showing</li>\r\n<li>I'll set my Knit Radar to 44 rows</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\t<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/122/scale.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n    \r\n    <img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/122/rulers1.jpg\" width=\"300\">\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 9715,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "How does this work?",
          "slug": "how-does-this-work",
          "order": 3,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 6349,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<b>NOTE 1:</b>As you are kntiting, if you need to adjust the position of the mylar, use the Plus and Minus Keys. Don't adjust manually<br><b>NOTE 2: </b>If you turn off the device (to save batteries) you'll need to reprogram the row gauge and re-position the row count on the device.<br><b>NOTE 3: </b>If you scrap off or rip rows, use the Pause key to stop the row counter temporarily.<br>",
              "legacyComponentId": 9725,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "imageGallery",
              "slides": [
